  "sop": {
    "title": "Sub-zero blend extraction — standard operating procedure",
    "preconditions": [
      "The carrier tank is above 20 000 L and the recovered carrier is above 15 000 L.",
      "The glycol loop is at -45 degC and holding pressure is below 60 bar.",
      "The nitrogen blanket on the crystalliser is below 2 % oxygen.",
      "The vacuum set is in one, two or three stage mode and the gauge reads below 100 mbar."
    ],
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "OP-10",
        "text": "Charge the extraction vessel with the carrier from the day tank and the biomass, and agitate at 20 degC for two hours.",
        "acceptance": "Agitator current is steady within 5 % of the reference run and the vessel is below 2 % oxygen."
      },
      {
        "id": "OP-20",
        "text": "Drain the extract through the 5 micron cloth into the crystalliser and swap the cloth bag.",
        "acceptance": "The differential pressure across the filter stays below 0.6 bar and the filtrate is clear."
      },
      {
        "id": "OP-30",
        "text": "Bring the crystalliser down to -40 degC at no more than 0.5 degC per minute and hold for twelve hours with the scraper turning every thirty minutes.",
        "acceptance": "The batch holds -40 degC for twelve hours with less than 1 degC of drift and the scraper current is steady."
      },
      {
        "id": "OP-40",
        "text": "Separate the mother liquor from the crystal cake at -40 degC and move the cake to the product drum.",
        "acceptance": "The cake temperature is below -25 degC at discharge and the assay of a sample matches the target within 2 %."
      },
      {
        "id": "OP-50",
        "text": "Strip the carrier from the mother liquor under vacuum, watching the azeotrope: stop the column when the condensate reaches 95 % pentane, because that is where the blend stops being the blend the client bought.",
        "acceptance": "The condensate is within 2 % of the azeotropic pentane composition and the residual solvent in the residue is below 1 %."
      },
      {
        "id": "OP-55",
        "text": "Condense the vapour on the four-shell bank, with the cascade coolant at -45 degC on the cold shell.",
        "acceptance": "The condensate temperature is below -10 degC and the tank gauge is below 100 mbar."
      },
      {
        "id": "OP-60",
        "text": "Return the recovered carrier to the day tank and re-assay it before it is used again.",
        "acceptance": "The recovered carrier assay is within 3 % of the make-up blend and the water is below 500 ppm."
      }
    ],
    "notes": [
      {
        "id": "N-1",
        "text": "Ethanol and n-pentane form a minimum-boiling azeotrope at 34.3 degC containing 95 % n-pentane by mass. Distillation cannot take the blend past it, so the recovered carrier is pentane-rich and carries about 5 % ethanol with it. If the client needs ethanol-rich carrier back, a pressure swing or a molecular sieve is needed; the skid's sieve stack is the second option.",
        "refersTo": "OP-50"
      },
      {
        "id": "N-2",
        "text": "The carrier arrives by tanker once a week. A 30 000 L tanker is roughly 20 batches of the 4 000 L extraction, so the day tank must hold a tanker and a half at peak, and the recovered carrier tank is the buffer against a carrier price move.",
        "refersTo": "V-101"
      },
      {
        "id": "N-3",
        "text": "CBD solubility falls steeply below -20 degC, which is the whole reason for the cold step. The exact curve at -40 degC is an assumption (A-02) and is the first thing to measure on the client's own plant.",
        "refersTo": "OP-30"
      },
      {
        "id": "N-4",
        "text": "The vapour from the recovery step carries cannabinoids. The scrubber on the exhaust line is not optional; the CRC carbon bed takes the cannabinoids and the zeolite takes the water.",
        "refersTo": "SC-101"
      }
    ]
  },
